\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs28\b STYLE GUIDE 1.16 (PARATEXT PLUGIN)\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b PURPOSE\b0\par
Style Guide is a Paratext plugin that helps a translation team fill in Biblica's style-guide modules. Each module is a Word document that lists topics (punctuation, footnotes, headings and so on), says what the NIV does, and leaves a yellow "Our Project" column for the team to describe its own practice.\par
The plugin reads the project's text and settings, works out what the project already does, and suggests an answer for every question it can. The team checks each suggestion, corrects or completes it, answers the remaining questions, and exports the filled-in Word document. The plugin never changes the project's text.\par
\par
\b THE MODULES\b0\par
\tab Punctuation\par
\tab Footnotes\par
\tab Headings\par
\tab Hyphenation\par
\tab Lists\par
\tab Numbers, Weights, Measures, Time\par
\tab Poetry\par
\tab Quotations\par
\tab Syntax, Grammar, Spelling\par
\tab Letters, Proclamations (draft)\par
\tab Markup and Layout (draft)\par
\tab Translation Considerations (draft)\par
The last three are drafts from Biblica; their questions may change in later versions of the documents. Some questions, such as those about grammar, the audience or the type of translation, cannot be answered from the text: the plugin says so, and the team answers them.\par
\par
\b INSTALLING\b0\par
1. Download Install_Phils_tools.exe from the Paratext_Plugins folder. If your browser warns about the file, choose to keep it.\par
2. Close Paratext.\par
3. Double-click Install_Phils_tools.exe. If Windows says it protected your PC, click "More info", then "Run anyway" (the installer is not signed yet).\par
4. Tick Style Guide and click "Install / update ticked". It installs into every Paratext 9 on the computer. If Windows asks for permission, click Yes. The same window updates the plugin later (its status then says "Update available") or removes it ("Remove ticked"), and its "User guide" button opens this guide.\par
\par
\b OPENING THE WINDOW\b0\par
Open the project in a Scripture window and choose Tools > Style Guide... The window opens and starts surveying the first module, Punctuation. While the survey runs, the line to the right of Rescan is orange and bold. Each module is surveyed the first time you choose it, which takes a few seconds (up to about 15 seconds for a large project).\par
